\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Current exact cellular-automaton pipeline.} The repository begins with the prompt-defined score target and a stage-indexed proof-carrying CA language. Every candidate is decoded without repair into the six-line witness format and then passed to the same rational-span verifier and synchronous trace engine. The verifier feeds three evidence streams: the exhaustive \(2\times 2\) corpus, the one-sided strip no-go atlas, and larger exact searches on score-relevant strip families. The net effect is a narrowed frontier: unilateral strip waves are ruled out in the audited classes, while coupled and macrocell families remain open.\relax }}{3}{figure.caption.1}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:pipeline}{{1}{3}{\textbf {Current exact cellular-automaton pipeline.} The repository begins with the prompt-defined score target and a stage-indexed proof-carrying CA language. Every candidate is decoded without repair into the six-line witness format and then passed to the same rational-span verifier and synchronous trace engine. The verifier feeds three evidence streams: the exhaustive \(2\times 2\) corpus, the one-sided strip no-go atlas, and larger exact searches on score-relevant strip families. The net effect is a narrowed frontier: unilateral strip waves are ruled out in the audited classes, while coupled and macrocell families remain open.\relax }{figure.caption.1}{}}
