\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Representative exact-valid \(2\times 2\) nucleus.} The left panel shows one witness from the exact-valid corpus, with full support on all three edge slots and three singleton seeds. The middle panel shows the unique first activation: one corner becomes forceable in layer \(0\). The right panel shows the resulting layer-\(1\) collapse of the other three vertices. All \(48\) exact-valid classes in the audited regime exhibit this same \(1+3\) two-layer trace skeleton up to the identity of the first corner.\relax }}{17}{figure.caption.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:nucleus}{{3}{17}{\textbf {Representative exact-valid \(2\times 2\) nucleus.} The left panel shows one witness from the exact-valid corpus, with full support on all three edge slots and three singleton seeds. The middle panel shows the unique first activation: one corner becomes forceable in layer \(0\). The right panel shows the resulting layer-\(1\) collapse of the other three vertices. All \(48\) exact-valid classes in the audited regime exhibit this same \(1+3\) two-layer trace skeleton up to the identity of the first corner.\relax }{figure.caption.5}{}}
